<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AQC recommends Marsford offer.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AQC recommends Marsford offer.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allied Queensland Coalfields Ltd said on Tuesday it had recommended shareholders accept the 78 cents per share takeover offer from Marsford Investments Pte Ltd.</p>
<p>Marsford is a unit of Hong Kong's Consolidated Electric Power Asia Ltd.  </p>
<p>Allied Queensland said its 43.36 percent shareholder Crusader Ltd, a unit of Clyde Petroleum Plc, has already said it would accept the Marsford offer. A spokesman for Allied Queensland said Crusader has sold its stake to Marsford.</p>
<p>At 11.55 a.m. (0055 GMT), Allied Queensland shares were one cent down at 78 cents a share on a turnover of 10.38 million shares, which represent almost half of the miner's issued capital.</p>
<p>On Monday, rival bidder Centennial Coal Co Ltd said it would not raise its 75 cents a share offer for the coal miner.  -- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
